.TH ROT13 1 "October 2026" "rot13 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rot13 \- ROT13 encoder and decoder
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rot13
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rot13
encodes or decodes text using the Caesar ROT13 symmetric substitution cipher.
Because ROT13 is symmetric (with an alphabet of 26 letters), applying the transformation
twice restores the original text.
.PP
If no \fIFILE\fR is specified, or when \fIFILE\fR is \fB\-\fR, input is read from standard input.
When multiple files are specified, they are processed in order and concatenated to standard output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-o\fR \fIFILE\fR
Write output directly to \fIFILE\fR instead of standard output.
.TP
\fB\-i\fR
Modify input file(s) in-place using atomic temporary file replacement while preserving permissions.
Symbolic links are resolved and their targets are updated.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Display version information and exit.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Display usage and help information and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Encode or decode a file to terminal:
.RS
.B rot13 document.txt
.RE
.PP
Stream input via pipe:
.RS
.B echo "Hello World" | rot13
.RE
.PP
Modify file in-place:
.RS
.B rot13 \-i notes.txt
.RE
.PP
Direct output to a specific target file:
.RS
.B rot13 \-o encoded.txt secret.txt
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success. Also returned upon receiving a broken pipe (\fBSIGPIPE\fR) in downstream pipelines.
.TP
.B 1
General error (file not found, directory passed as input, invalid arguments).
.TP
.B 130
Process terminated by interruption signal (\fBSIGINT\fR / Ctrl+C).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tr (1),
.BR cat (1),
.BR sed (1)
